A five-year scenario about AI and Europe.

Some early evidence suggests that managers are most successful in using Claude Code for coding tasks. The idea is that management is an AI superpower because clearly specifying what you want, how to do it, and what good looks like is key to effectively using agents.

@emollick: "Management is an AI superpower—being able to specify goals and expectations clearly helps in leveraging agents effectively."

Thriving in a world of agents.

Interesting stuff. And the visualization at the end is worth trying.

@AnthropicAI: "New Anthropic research shows a global workspace in language models. Of everything happening in your brain right now, only a tiny fraction is consciously accessible—thoughts you can describe, hold in mind, and reason with. We found a strikingly similar divide inside Claude."

The linked research reveals a global workspace in language models, highlighting parallels with human consciousness and internal processing.
